When ethanedioyl chloride is reacted with silver ethanedioate, $\text{AgO}_2\text{CCO}_2\text{Ag}$, in ethoxyethane at $-30^{\circ}\text{C}$, an oxide of carbon, **L**, is formed. The molecule of **L** has no overall dipole and has molecular formula $\text{C}_4\text{O}_6$.

The carbon-13 NMR spectrum of a solution of **L** in ethoxyethane, $\text{CH}_3\text{CH}_2\text{OCH}_2\text{CH}_3$, is shown below.

{{figure:pdf_visual_02.png}}
